From b602a02764a783b2cfeadfbe50341663b2d06111 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JoshuaHayesWasHere <josh.hayes121@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:30:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(web): a jstack "asks you" row opens what it asks

A task with no thread that waits on the user opened its home, which is
often the thread already open, so the click did nothing. It now unfolds
the ask with the gate's default and the task's brief. A held row shows
in review, where it was dropped from the tree.
